1. **Stitching** now uses `xScale`/`yScale` so that each source pixel maps exactly once horizontally and vertically – preserving the original pixel count.
2. **Triangle rendering** now applies separate X/Y scales when mapping from stitched canvas space back into projected pixel space, so the reprojection no longer forces square pixels.
